{"authored" [{"question" "q-37649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the system\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-2{x}_{3}=-2 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=2 \\\\ 3{x}_{1}-6{x}_{3}=-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce the augmented matrix $M$ of the system to row echelon form." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "df8799a719651e1b1f3abe0c80672b9314b4130e6e569d7ae708c79c40af307c" "basis" 1524 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The augmented matrix for this system is\n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nReducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -2 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 3 & 0 & -6 & -6\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+(-3){R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "df8799a719651e1b1f3abe0c80672b9314b4130e6e569d7ae708c79c40af307c" "basis" 1524 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37649" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b3e78a9c84e0212da886c5543cbe7115ae579a917b76e508cf22103c3595052f" "basis" 1524 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "df8799a719651e1b1f3abe0c80672b9314b4130e6e569d7ae708c79c40af307c" "basis" 1524 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 0 & 2 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "df8799a719651e1b1f3abe0c80672b9314b4130e6e569d7ae708c79c40af307c" "basis" 1524 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "df8799a719651e1b1f3abe0c80672b9314b4130e6e569d7ae708c79c40af307c" "basis" 1524 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & -2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "df8799a719651e1b1f3abe0c80672b9314b4130e6e569d7ae708c79c40af307c" "basis" 1524 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "df8799a719651e1b1f3abe0c80672b9314b4130e6e569d7ae708c79c40af307c" "basis" 1524 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-37649" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "M∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & -4 & -4 \\\\ 0 & -1 & 2 & -2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "df8799a719651e1b1f3abe0c80672b9314b4130e6e569d7ae708c79c40af307c" "basis" 1524 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73913" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 & 7 & -9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "df8799a719651e1b1f3abe0c80672b9314b4130e6e569d7ae708c79c40af307c" "basis" 1524 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73913" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x-2y+7z=-9 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince any numbers $x,y,z$ form a solution of the final two equations $0x+0y+0z=0,$ we can remove these equations from the system. So, our system now consists of just a single equation:\n\n$$\nx-2y+7z=-9\n$$\n\nThe basic variables are the variables whose coefficients are pivots. In this case, the basic variable is $x$, and we have two free variables $y$ and $z.$ That means we need to find $x$ in terms of $y,z.$ Doing this, we get\n\n$$\nx=-9+2y-7z.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-9+2y-7z \\\\ y=y \\\\ z=z,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $y$, $z$ (free variables) are arbitrary numbers.\n\nIn vector form, the solution can be written as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-9+2y-7z \\\\ y \\\\ z\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "df8799a719651e1b1f3abe0c80672b9314b4130e6e569d7ae708c79c40af307c" "basis" 1524 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73913" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b3e78a9c84e0212da886c5543cbe7115ae579a917b76e508cf22103c3595052f" "basis" 1524 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73913" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "df8799a719651e1b1f3abe0c80672b9314b4130e6e569d7ae708c79c40af307c" "basis" 1524 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73913" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "df8799a719651e1b1f3abe0c80672b9314b4130e6e569d7ae708c79c40af307c" "basis" 1524 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73913" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "df8799a719651e1b1f3ab