/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73913" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "[\\begin{aligned}-9 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+y[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]+z[\\begin{aligned}-7 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}],\\,y,z\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty )"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "df8799a719651e1b1f3abe0c80672b9314b4130e6e569d7ae708c79c40af307c" "basis" 1524 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73955" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 & -2 & -5 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -2 & -3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & -5\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind the general solution of the linear system represented by the matrix." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "df8799a719651e1b1f3abe0c80672b9314b4130e6e569d7ae708c79c40af307c" "basis" 1524 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-73955" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "The system corresponding to $M$ is\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}4x+y-2z=-5 \\\\ 0x+2y-2z=-3 \\\\ 0x+0y+0z=-5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince there are no such numbers $x,y,z$ that form a solution of the final equation $0x+0y+0z=-5,$ we can conclude that our system has no solution." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14041677/state.json" "file_sha256" "df8799a719651e1b1f3abe0c80672b9314b4130e6e569d7ae708c79c40af307c" "basis" 1524 "verification" "/home/jake